rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All runtime-native workflows must conform to the CAS Workflow Execution
    Model, ensuring clear separation of concerns between orchestration, reasoning,
    and knowledge access.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
    validation_type: governance
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures consistent interpretation between pattern maturity and decision
    lifecycle stages, preventing the conflation of knowledge evolution with governance
    status.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that all patterns are initially created as supporting by default
    to ensure validation through evidence before promotion to core foundational primitives.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Prohibits the merging or consolidation of patterns across different architectural
    layers to maintain separation between governance, execution, and reliability concerns.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires that any pattern promotion to the core layer is supported by strong
    evidence from multiple sources to ensure stability and reliability.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes Architecture Work as the authoritative source of planning state,
    requiring all generated artifacts to derive their status from it.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
    validation_type: quality
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Enforces the use of a structured YAML schema for all architectural decisions
    (ADR) to enable machine processing and consistent rendering.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires projects to participate in a shared Knowledge Workspace and prohibits
    the creation of duplicate global or runtime governance structures.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the semantic contract for architectural language, distinguishing
    clearly between intent, decisions, and system state to ensure alignment.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that all patterns derived from heuristics must include at least
    one linked signal as evidence to ensure grounding in observed insights.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the precedence model (Global > Project > Prompt) used to resolve
    conflicts between rules originating from different sources.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains human-in-the-loop control by requiring all system-proposed architectural
    decisions to be explicitly accepted or rejected by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: States that generated governance artifacts summarize authoritative sources
    and must not become the primary source of truth themselves.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
    validation_type: governance
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that architecture decisions are recorded and updated only in ADRs,
    with all other representations being derived from those records.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines strict criteria for signal promotion, including recurrence, system
    impact, reusability, and stability, supported by observable evidence.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires all architectural decisions to be persisted as structured ADRs
    before being reflected in maps (AEM) or other governance artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires the lifecycle stage of architecture items to be derived from their
    decision status, preventing items from being marked as 'DONE' prematurely.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures the Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) reflects and never contradicts
    decisions formally recorded in Architecture Decision Records (ADR).
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Limits core pattern classification to foundational architectural primitives,
    rejecting specific implementations or context-specific strategies.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
